<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="49520" href="schedule/2008/fall/FIN/490/49520.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2008" href="schedule/2008.xml">2008</calendarYear><term id="120088" href="schedule/2008/fall.xml">Fall 2008</term><subject id="FIN" href="schedule/2008/fall/FIN.xml">Finance</subject><course id="490" href="schedule/2008/fall/FIN/490.xml">Special Topics in Finance</course></parents><sectionNumber>FM </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Financial Modeling</sectionTitle><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Financial Modeling concentrates on developing the skills and techniques required to build financial models using Excel. Students will use excel features and built-in functions to build models in the Time Value of Money, Financial Statements Forecasting, Value at Risk, Ratio Analysis, Bond Pricing and Duration, and Options Pricing.  STUDENTS SHOULD CONTACT PROF. OLTHETEN AT OLTHETEN@UIUC.EDU ABOUT REGISTERING.  Priority will be given students who have completed both FIN 311 and FIN 321.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2008-08-25Z</startDate><endDate>2008-12-10Z</endDate><specialApproval>Instructor Approval Required</specialApproval><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>10:00 AM</start><end>11:20 AM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>24</roomNumber><buildingName>David Kinley Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Oltheten" firstName="E">Oltheten, E</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>